-- title:
--   Adjoining a primitive q-th root of unity to a complete DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 3$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain with maximal ideal generated by $q$, and let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, an $A_0$-algebra with $\mathrm{algebraMap}\ A_0\ A$ injective and $A$ module-finite over $A_0$, containing an element $\zeta$ which is a primitive $q$-th root of unity and satisfies $A_0[\zeta] = A$ (the $A_0$-subalgebra generated by $\zeta$ is everything), with maximal ideal generated by some $\varpi \in A$. Let $W_0$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, complete with respect to its maximal ideal, with maximal ideal generated by $q$, and equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure. Let $R_0$ be a local ring which is a $W_0$-algebra via a local homomorphism, and let $\sigma_0 : A \to R_0$ be a ring homomorphism satisfying $\sigma_0(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ A_0\ A\ a_0) = \mathrm{algebraMap}\ W_0\ R_0(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ A_0\ W_0\ a_0)$ for all $a_0 \in A_0$. Then there exist a type $W_1$ carrying the structure of a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete with respect to its maximal ideal, together with ring homomorphisms $j_1 : W_0 \to W_1$, $\sigma : A \to W_1$ and a local homomorphism $\iota_1 : W_1 \to R_0$, such that $j_1$ followed by $\iota_1$ equals $\mathrm{algebraMap}\ W_0\ R_0$, $\sigma$ followed by $\iota_1$ equals $\sigma_0$, $\sigma$ and $j_1$ agree on the image of $A_0$, the maximal ideal of $W_1$ is generated by $\sigma(\varpi)$, and $\sigma(\varpi)^{q-1} = \varepsilon_1 q$ in $W_1$ for some unit $\varepsilon_1$ of $W_1$.
--
--   This is the construction of the coefficient ring $W_1 = W_0[\zeta_q]$, a totally ramified extension of degree $q-1$ of the complete discrete valuation ring $W_0$ with uniformiser the image of $\varpi$ and with $\varpi^{q-1}$ equal to $q$ up to a unit, realised inside any given local $W_0$-algebra $R_0$ carrying a homomorphism from $A$. It is used in the analysis of the completed local rings of modular curves at supersingular points with full level structure, where such a ring of coefficients containing $q$-th roots of unity and a compatible map to the ambient local ring is required.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsPrimitiveRoot_exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_isAdicComplete_ringHom_comp_eq_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pow_sub_one_eq_mul_of_adjoin_eq_top.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
